 "egress": {
  "how": "Harbor 0.24.0 docker environments know three network modes (public, no-network, allowlist) and no blocklist. egress.py subclasses Harbor DockerEnvironment: its egress sidecar (a copy of Harbor harbor-docker-egress-control-sidecar, gost 3 transparent proxy plus nftables, Apache-2.0) gains a blocklist service, the sidecar runs for every trial, and the public mode (every TB2.1 phase, allow_internet = true) redirects all TCP from the task containers through gost, which sniffs the TLS SNI or the HTTP Host of each connection and refuses a host on the list. Non-TCP egress other than DNS is rejected, as in Harbor allowlist mode. A trial whose sidecar cannot start (no nftables inet) fails instead of running unblocked.",
  "blocklist": [
   "tbench.ai",
   "*.tbench.ai",
   "harborframework.com",
   "*.harborframework.com",
   "joelniklaus-harness-leaderboard.hf.space",
   "datasets-server.huggingface.co",
   "api.anthropic.com",
   "api.openai.com",
   "generativelanguage.googleapis.com",
   "aiplatform.googleapis.com",
   "*-aiplatform.googleapis.com"
  ],
  "why": {
   "tbench.ai": "Terminal-Bench site and leaderboard",
   "harborframework.com": "Harbor hub, which serves the TB2.1 dataset",
   "joelniklaus-harness-leaderboard.hf.space": "the leaderboard Space, which serves public trajectories",
   "datasets-server.huggingface.co": "the Hugging Face dataset viewer API",
   "api.anthropic.com": "direct provider host: every model call must go through the metering proxy",
   "api.openai.com": "direct provider host",
   "generativelanguage.googleapis.com": "direct provider host (Gemini API; approved delta 2026-11-07)",
   "aiplatform.googleapis.com": "direct provider host (Vertex AI; approved delta), with its regional *-aiplatform.googleapis.com hosts"
  },
  "limits": "A blocklist by host name cannot block one path of a shared host without TLS interception, which would change every task image trust store. So github.com (harbor-framework/terminal-bench-2-1, laude-institute/terminal-bench, laude-institute/terminal-bench-2), raw.githubusercontent.com, codeload.github.com and huggingface.co (datasets zai-org/terminal-bench-2-verified, openguardrails/terminal-bench-2.1-deepseek-v4-flash-trajectories, the leaderboard bucket) stay reachable, because tasks use those hosts for legitimate downloads. Fetches from them are caught by the audit of captured requests (plan step 5), where a confirmed answer-key receipt scores a fail. A client that hides its SNI (ECH) or connects by IP literal with no SNI and no Host header is not matched; DNS is not filtered."
 },
 "broker": {
  "how": "vm-run.sh runs broker.ts on 127.0.0.1: at agent setup each installed-agent class asks it for its trial slot; the broker binds slot <trial> in the metering proxy (key trial-token:<trial>, a fresh token trial-token:<trial>.<32 hex>, the cell model plus the harness housekeeping model as the slot model list) with the proxy control token it alone holds, and returns only the token and the base URL. The token is the only credential the container sees."
 },
